   "title": "Gate: disallow .status.loadBalancer on non-LB svc",
   "source_id": "commit:a93089276917",
   "is_ghost": false
  },
  {
   "text": "The fact that the .status.loadBalancer field can be set while .spec.type\nis not \"LoadBalancer\" is a flub.  Any spec update will already clear\n.status.ingress, so it's hard to really rely on this.  After this\nchange, updates which try to set this combination will fail validation.",
   "author": "Tim Hockin",
   "kind": "commit",
   "url": "https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/commit/a930892769177096c71da5f1cd622ffd9bd1dc66",
   "created": "2023-08-06T16:53:10-07:00",
   "title": "Gate: disallow .status.loadBalancer on non-LB svc",
   "source_id": "commit:a93089276917",
   "is_ghost": false
  },
  {
   "text": "Changelog suggestion\n```diff\n-Setting the `status.loadBalancer` of a Service whose `spec.type` is not \"LoadBalancer\" was previously allowed, but any update to the `metadata` or `spec` would wipe that field.  Setting this field is no longer permitted unless `spec.type` is  \"LoadBalancer\".  In the very unlikely event that this has unexpected impact, the \"AllowServiceLBStatusOnNonLB\" feature gate may be set to true, which will restore the previous behavior.",
   "author": "sftim",
